Leave your waitress alone.

1927
01:37:05.490 --> 01:37:07.630
In general, leave your waitresses alone.

1928
01:37:07.850 --> 01:37:08.830
Come on, everybody.

1929
01:37:09.210 --> 01:37:13.650
Oh, but before we move on from this table scene, I want to give a shout out to the guest

1930
01:37:13.650 --> 01:37:15.950
actress who plays the woman at the table.

1931
01:37:16.330 --> 01:37:16.630
Yes.

1932
01:37:16.990 --> 01:37:19.510
Annie Sertik, who gives Dwight so much sass.

1933
01:37:19.970 --> 01:37:20.530
Yes.

1934
01:37:21.030 --> 01:37:22.990
Guys, she's amazing.

1935
01:37:22.990 --> 01:37:30.630
I feel like she's only got the one line to Dwight, but her expressions and all of her

1936
01:37:30.630 --> 01:37:32.750
reactions during the scene are so great.

1937
01:37:33.250 --> 01:37:35.930
And she is a company member at the Groundlings.

1938
01:37:36.090 --> 01:37:39.050
She's had recurring roles on Silicon Valley and Two Broke Girls.

1939
01:37:39.290 --> 01:37:44.610
And I did a deep dive on her IMDb, and I found this little interesting bit of trivia, Angela.

1940
01:37:44.950 --> 01:37:45.110
What?

1941
01:37:46.110 --> 01:37:50.490
She was on Curb Your Enthusiasm, where she played, quote unquote, buffet woman.

1942
01:37:51.330 --> 01:37:54.650
And then she was on Cougar Town playing female chef.

1943
01:37:55.210 --> 01:37:58.490
I just thought it was interesting that she's had three guest roles involving food.

1944
01:37:58.750 --> 01:38:05.150
I'm also really envious that she got to play buffet woman because that's the role of my

1945
01:38:05.150 --> 01:38:05.650
dreaMs.

1946
01:38:09.350 --> 01:38:10.690
Yes, exactly.

1947
01:38:11.210 --> 01:38:11.470
All right.

1948
01:38:11.570 --> 01:38:13.270
We're back now at the parties.

1949
01:38:13.470 --> 01:38:15.010
Angela's is not going well.

1950
01:38:15.150 --> 01:38:16.050
It's pretty boring.

1951
01:38:16.050 --> 01:38:19.190
Phyllis is, like, desperate to get out of this party.

1952
01:38:19.430 --> 01:38:23.270
She really is one of my favorite things in this whole episode.

1953
01:38:23.610 --> 01:38:26.750
Her yearning to be at the other party is so brilliant.

1954
01:38:26.950 --> 01:38:28.190
Phyllis is so brilliant.

1955
01:38:28.410 --> 01:38:32.570
And there is a deleted scene that's great that really would have amplified this.

1956
01:38:33.210 --> 01:38:37.830
She pours herself, like, a drink, and it's, like, ginger ale.

1957
01:38:37.970 --> 01:38:41.030
And she says, oh, there's not a lot of fizz in this.

1958
01:38:41.170 --> 01:38:43.110
And she starts to make her way to the door.

1959
01:38:43.170 --> 01:38:43.750
And I'm like, no, no, no.

1960
01:38:43.750 --> 01:38:46.010
And she goes, I might should get some more ginger ale.

1961
01:38:46.070 --> 01:38:46.850
And I'm like, no, no, no.

1962
01:38:46.950 --> 01:38:48.250
And I block her from leaving.

1963
01:38:48.410 --> 01:38:49.550
I was like, I'll go get it.

1964
01:38:49.650 --> 01:38:50.090
You stay.

1965
01:38:51.870 --> 01:38:52.970
That is amazing.

1966
01:38:53.270 --> 01:38:57.850
But her reaction when she pours in, she's like, there's not a lot of fizz.

1967
01:38:58.270 --> 01:39:01.670
It's like you see her plotting to get out of the conference room.

1968
01:39:01.670 --> 01:39:10.710
Well, I also quite enjoyed, in this scene, Hannah, if you look at her in the background, she is, like, really examining the napkins.

1969
01:39:11.230 --> 01:39:15.290
She is giving your napkins, like, the third degree.

1970
01:39:15.510 --> 01:39:17.830
I'm sorry she's not going to stick around longer.

1971
01:39:17.930 --> 01:39:20.730
Well, we'll get to that in future episodes.

1972
01:39:20.930 --> 01:39:21.190
Yes.

1973
01:39:21.190 --> 01:39:21.770
All right.

1974
01:39:21.930 --> 01:39:29.150
Well, Pam and Karen's party is a big hit, except the karaoke machine won't work because they don't have the right cord.

1975
01:39:29.630 --> 01:39:33.890
But don't worry, because Daryl is going to go get his keyboard.

1976
01:39:33.890 --> 01:39:36.890
And then there's this scene that I absolutely love.

1977
01:39:37.050 --> 01:39:44.110
As Daryl walks past the conference room, he's like, hey, when you're done with your meeting, there's a party in the break room.

1978
01:39:44.790 --> 01:39:52.990
But it's the way Craig says it, because Craig is like, hey, guys, when you get done with your meeting, it's like he doesn't quite know what to call it.

1979
01:39:53.090 --> 01:39:53.850
What are they doing?

1980
01:39:54.070 --> 01:39:54.210
He's like, a meeting?

1981
01:39:56.010 --> 01:39:58.830
You should come to the break room because we're having an actual party.

1982
01:39:59.250 --> 01:40:00.370
And I love it.

1983
01:40:00.370 --> 01:40:08.350
And that's when, at 28 minutes, 24 seconds, Phyllis is standing in the doorway, and she's sort of gazing at the other party.

1984
01:40:08.430 --> 01:40:10.610
And then Ryan comes to get his jacket.

1985
01:40:10.830 --> 01:40:12.050
She's like, are you cold?

1986
01:40:12.270 --> 01:40:13.050
That'll help.

1987
01:40:13.550 --> 01:40:14.750
Is it cold in there?

1988
01:40:15.710 --> 01:40:16.550
You know what?

1989
01:40:16.670 --> 01:40:17.570
That was an improv.

1990
01:40:17.990 --> 01:40:19.150
That was not in script.

1991
01:40:19.430 --> 01:40:20.170
Stop it.

1992
01:40:20.230 --> 01:40:20.490
Yes.

1993
01:40:20.770 --> 01:40:21.250
Which part?

1994
01:40:21.410 --> 01:40:22.290
The final line?

1995
01:40:22.470 --> 01:40:25.090
It was scripted that Ryan would come and get his jacket.

1996
01:40:26.670 --> 01:40:30.610
And that Phyllis just says something like, how is it in there?

1997
01:40:30.750 --> 01:40:32.010
And then he's like, huh?

1998
01:40:32.470 --> 01:40:33.870
And that was the end of the scene.

1999
01:40:33.990 --> 01:40:34.830
And then he walks away.

2000
01:40:34.990 --> 01:40:38.170
So Phyllis being like, maybe that'll help.

2001
01:40:38.350 --> 01:40:39.530
Is it cold in there?

2002
01:40:40.970 --> 01:40:42.130
That was Phyllis.

2003
01:40:42.770 --> 01:40:44.310
Well, her maybe that would help.

2004
01:40:44.510 --> 01:40:45.910
Like, that had me fall out of the chair.

2005
01:40:46.070 --> 01:40:49.470
Her runner is just absolutely one of my favorites in this whole episode.

2006
01:40:50.210 --> 01:40:57.130
So now the guys return from Benihana and they have brought waitresses with them.

2007
01:40:57.290 --> 01:41:03.350
So we covered a little bit of the Benihana waitress storyline with Jen, but we did not

2008
01:41:03.350 --> 01:41:09.010
really talk about this and we got a lot of fan questions from Emma Bloom, Kelsey K, Kayla

2009
01:41:09.010 --> 01:41:14.890
Bass, Abby Roll, Tanessa Lee, Samantha Munden, and many others want to know, why do the actresses

2010
01:41:14.890 --> 01:41:19.930
playing the Benihana waitresses change when Michael and Andy bring them back to the office?

2011
01:41:20.250 --> 01:41:25.750
Is that supposed to feed into the ongoing joke that Michael and Andy can't tell them apart?

2012
01:41:27.230 --> 01:41:34.850
So no, the idea here was simply that Michael and Andy couldn't land the original waitresses

2013
01:41:34.850 --> 01:41:36.530
that they'd been flirting with all night.

2014
01:41:36.810 --> 01:41:43.550
And then they managed to get these two younger, kind of more naive waitresses to come back with

2015
01:41:43.550 --> 01:41:44.590
them to the office.

2016
01:41:44.930 --> 01:41:50.830
And in the script, it says Michael and Andy walk in, not with Cindy and her hot friend,

2017
01:41:50.830 --> 01:41:55.730
but with two other 20 to 25 year old Asian American waitresses.

2018
01:41:56.230 --> 01:42:01.910
So the idea was that these two older, sophisticated women would never go back to a party.

2019
01:42:02.450 --> 01:42:09.450
But these two younger gals, college age gals, would be like, oh, yeah, like free drinks.

2020
01:42:09.690 --> 01:42:10.110
We'll go.

2021
01:42:10.410 --> 01:42:10.750
Free drinks.

2022
01:42:11.110 --> 01:42:12.130
Like they're more up for it.

2023
01:42:12.130 --> 01:42:12.530
Yeah.

2024
01:42:12.830 --> 01:42:13.270
Free drinks.

2025
01:42:13.390 --> 01:42:15.210
And Michael's like, and I have a present for you.

2026
01:42:15.350 --> 01:42:16.050
It's a bicycle.

2027
01:42:17.310 --> 01:42:17.830
Yes.

2028
01:42:18.210 --> 01:42:19.370
And she's thrilled.

2029
01:42:19.630 --> 01:42:20.990
She's like, I love it.

2030
01:42:21.290 --> 01:42:21.570
Yeah.

2031
01:42:21.790 --> 01:42:25.930
Well, I have a background catch at 29 minutes when they walk into the office.

2032
01:42:26.390 --> 01:42:28.650
The girls have on a lot of makeup.

2033
01:42:28.650 --> 01:42:32.510
And then at 29 minutes, 12 seconds later, no makeup.

2034
01:42:32.790 --> 01:42:33.610
What happened?

2035
01:42:33.830 --> 01:42:36.310
Well, Angela, a lot of other people noticed this as well.

2036
01:42:37.030 --> 01:42:39.950
Sonia Maria Raposa wrote in with a theory.

2037
01:42:39.950 --> 01:42:46.170
Oh, she thinks that they appear with makeup at first because that's how Michael perceives them

2038
01:42:46.170 --> 01:42:47.450
to be because he's drunk.

2039
01:42:47.690 --> 01:42:51.210
And then they appear with no makeup because that's what they truly look like.

2040
01:42:51.530 --> 01:42:52.550
It's not the case.

2041
01:42:52.930 --> 01:42:56.210
Jen did a little bit of a deep dive, and she actually found an interview that her and Greg

2042
01:42:56.210 --> 01:43:00.750
did on an office panel about this exact thing.

2043
01:43:01.170 --> 01:43:03.890
And she said, basically, it was a continuity error.

2044
01:43:04.510 --> 01:43:05.230
Yeah, exactly.

2045
01:43:05.470 --> 01:43:08.670
She was telling us that the first day that they worked, they put makeup on them.

2046
01:43:08.890 --> 01:43:12.290
Then they watched the dailies, and they were like, well, wait, that doesn't really track

2047
01:43:12.290 --> 01:43:16.710
for who they are in the show as their characters, these younger college girls.

2048
01:43:17.190 --> 01:43:20.130
And, you know, they shouldn't look that sophisticated.

2049
01:43:20.250 --> 01:43:24.770
So the next time they worked, they toned down, didn't have them have makeup on.

2050
01:43:24.770 --> 01:43:26.450
So it was as simple as that.

2051
01:43:26.710 --> 01:43:31.870
They really wanted to drive home this idea that these were college girls to kind of further

2052
01:43:31.870 --> 01:43:38.270
emphasize how ridiculous Michael's infatuation and belief that he's found his true love is.

2053
01:43:38.590 --> 01:43:38.870
Yeah.

2054
01:43:38.990 --> 01:43:43.790
And Michael now starts going around the office and introducing Nikki as his new girlfriend.

2055
01:43:44.190 --> 01:43:46.830
Everyone is like, girlfriend.

2056
01:43:47.770 --> 01:43:48.150
Huh.

2057
01:43:48.590 --> 01:43:49.110
Really?

2058
01:43:49.310 --> 01:43:53.150
Well, they realized pretty quickly that Angela's party is super lame.

2059
01:43:53.150 --> 01:43:57.110
And as they leave, Nikki takes one of Angela's decorations.

2060
01:43:57.330 --> 01:43:59.850
And Angela is ticked off.

2061
01:43:59.970 --> 01:44:02.790
And she insults her with the Hello Kitty backpack line.

2062
01:44:02.910 --> 01:44:04.810
It's just a horrible thing to say.

2063
01:44:04.970 --> 01:44:09.910
And Michael wants to get Nikki away from Angela as soon as possible.

2064
01:44:10.290 --> 01:44:15.730
So he takes her to the really fun party in the break room.

2065
01:44:15.730 --> 01:44:18.370
We have Kevin singing karaoke.

2066
01:44:19.150 --> 01:44:19.830
Yeah.

2067
01:44:19.830 --> 01:44:23.890
Go to 31 minutes, 14 seconds, and please watch Ryan.

2068
01:44:24.030 --> 01:44:26.550
It is the most animated I've ever seen him.

2069
01:44:26.690 --> 01:44:31.010
He's like swaying back and forth singing like, you gotta know.

2070
01:44:31.330 --> 01:44:32.690
He's like so into it.

2071
01:44:32.750 --> 01:44:33.650
I'm like, what's happening, Ryan?

2072
01:44:33.770 --> 01:44:34.610
Is he drunk too?

2073
01:44:34.850 --> 01:44:37.390
Well, I did have a fan question from this scene.

2074
01:44:37.530 --> 01:44:37.670
Okay.

2075
01:44:37.790 --> 01:44:43.050
From Sasha Lara, who wants to know, does Craig Robinson play the keyboard in real life?

2076
01:44:43.210 --> 01:44:44.550
Oh, Sasha, yes, he does.

2077
01:44:44.970 --> 01:44:46.190
He definitely does.

2078
01:44:46.430 --> 01:44:48.190
Oh, he's phenomenal.

2079
01:44:48.190 --> 01:44:48.950
Are you kidding?

2080
01:44:49.550 --> 01:44:50.370
He's amazing.

2081
01:44:50.690 --> 01:44:55.830
And in those scenes on the show, when Craig would get out the keyboard, it really did turn

2082
01:44:55.830 --> 01:44:56.550
into a party.

2083
01:44:56.830 --> 01:44:58.730
Like, that was really fun to shoot.

2084
01:44:58.850 --> 01:45:02.150
Angela, I'm sorry that you weren't in there, but we were having an amazing time.

2085
01:45:02.350 --> 01:45:05.990
And between takes, Craig would play and we would sing.

2086
01:45:05.990 --> 01:45:08.290
And Kate would sing show tunes.

2087
01:45:08.690 --> 01:45:14.190
And I mean, it was like, it was exactly as much fun as you would imagine it would be.

2088
01:45:14.330 --> 01:45:17.890
I'm bummed I wasn't in that scene to be able to hang out with you guys like that.

2089
01:45:18.010 --> 01:45:20.870
But I cherish the times we were all in the conference room.

2090
01:45:21.250 --> 01:45:26.410
And if Craig, for, you know, in the latter years, he was in the main office bullpen and

2091
01:45:26.410 --> 01:45:29.010
he and Kate would start singing.

2092
01:45:29.310 --> 01:45:32.530
And Ed, I have found a video on my phone.

2093
01:45:32.730 --> 01:45:33.830
Oh, my God, Jenna.

2094
01:45:34.070 --> 01:45:35.610
It's us in the conference room.

2095
01:45:35.910 --> 01:45:38.230
And they just start making up a song.

2096
01:45:38.430 --> 01:45:40.990
And like, oh, and everyone is singing.

2097
01:45:40.990 --> 01:45:42.090
And it's so great.

2098
01:45:42.310 --> 01:45:43.450
I love it.

2099
01:45:44.330 --> 01:45:46.210
Those are some of my favorite memories.

2100
01:45:46.550 --> 01:45:47.770
I'll text you the video.

2101
01:45:47.930 --> 01:45:50.770
Ladies, should we go back to your super sad party?

2102
01:45:50.770 --> 01:45:52.350
No, I guess.

2103
01:45:53.070 --> 01:45:54.630
Angela's having a horrible day.

2104
01:45:54.810 --> 01:45:59.310
But a big thing happens here, which is that Dwight holds Angela's hand.

2105
01:45:59.550 --> 01:46:00.150
I know.

2106
01:46:00.390 --> 01:46:02.330
It's like a very, very small moment.

2107
01:46:02.330 --> 01:46:04.590
She's holding her boombox in her lap.

2108
01:46:05.070 --> 01:46:06.410
And they hold hands.

2109
01:46:06.630 --> 01:46:11.670
Well, this is when then Karen enters and announces that Dwight won the raffle,

2110
01:46:11.670 --> 01:46:17.530
which, of course, is like a super passive aggressive thing to try to lure Dwight into the

2111
01:46:17.530 --> 01:46:18.470
fun of their party.

2112
01:46:19.070 --> 01:46:27.950
And as Dwight is excitedly opening the gift, Pam kind of clocks Angela's sadness and pulls

2113
01:46:27.950 --> 01:46:31.390
Karen aside and says, I feel kind of bad for Angela.

2114
01:46:31.830 --> 01:46:32.330
Hold up.

2115
01:46:32.990 --> 01:46:35.050
Did Dwight really not win the raffle?

2116
01:46:36.230 --> 01:46:37.070
No, lady.

2117
01:46:37.370 --> 01:46:39.910
We just did that to try to lure him to our party.

2118
01:46:40.190 --> 01:46:41.070
This whole time.

2119
01:46:41.330 --> 01:46:42.970
I mean, when did he have time to enter the raffle?

2120
01:46:43.150 --> 01:46:43.630
I don't know.

2121
01:46:43.710 --> 01:46:45.870
But this whole time, I thought he won the raffle.

2122
01:46:46.890 --> 01:46:48.990
Oh, I was like, oh, my God, Dwight won the raffle.

2123
01:46:50.130 --> 01:46:57.030
I mean, I always took it to be like another like how we lured Kevin away from your party.

2124
01:46:57.250 --> 01:47:01.810
This is how we were going to lure Dwight away by coming into your party and like trying to

2125
01:47:01.810 --> 01:47:02.390
poach him.

2126
01:47:02.510 --> 01:47:03.230
Oh, my God.

2127
01:47:03.450 --> 01:47:04.050
Mean girls.

2128
01:47:04.270 --> 01:47:06.830
Here I am all naive thinking like, way to go, Dwight.

2129
01:47:07.410 --> 01:47:11.570
I mean, I don't think he won the raffle.

2130
01:47:11.570 --> 01:47:16.650
No, that was my take on it was that it was a little bit of a mean girls moment on Pam

2131
01:47:16.650 --> 01:47:17.590
and Karen's part.

2132
01:47:17.750 --> 01:47:21.890
But you get Karen to come around and now you guys try to make amends.

2133
01:47:22.910 --> 01:47:23.690
We do.

2134
01:47:23.970 --> 01:47:28.850
And by the way, I mean, we may be passive aggressively let Dwight win the raffle, but

2135
01:47:28.850 --> 01:47:31.630
you stole our power cord and hit it in a plant.

2136
01:47:31.890 --> 01:47:32.330
I know.

2137
01:47:32.410 --> 01:47:36.770
I was about to say you guys faked a raffle and I'm shocked by that.

2138
01:47:36.770 --> 01:47:37.750
How could you?

2139
01:47:37.930 --> 01:47:42.050
But I full on stole the cable and hit it in a plant.

2140
01:47:42.590 --> 01:47:45.550
Yes, you sabotaged our karaoke machine.

2141
01:47:45.770 --> 01:47:54.450
OK, so now the parties have merged and the karaoke machine has its cord and we open with

2142
01:47:54.450 --> 01:47:57.450
Andy and Michael singing Your Body is a Wonderland.

2143
01:47:58.510 --> 01:48:03.590
Michael is not sure which waitress is his girlfriend here, so he's singing to both of them.

2144
01:48:03.590 --> 01:48:08.450
So we talked a little bit with Jen about all the different songs that people sing for karaoke,

2145
01:48:08.470 --> 01:48:10.010
but we did not touch on this one.

2146
01:48:10.110 --> 01:48:11.970
And I have some really good trivia about it.

2147
01:48:12.070 --> 01:48:12.610
Let's hear it.

2148
01:48:12.750 --> 01:48:18.350
So we reached out to John Mayer to ask him if we could use his song, Your Body is a Wonderland.

2149
01:48:18.390 --> 01:48:22.590
And it was actually BJ Novak who reached out to him because BJ knew him.

2150
01:48:22.770 --> 01:48:23.370
Knows him.

2151
01:48:23.530 --> 01:48:23.590
Right?

2152
01:48:23.610 --> 01:48:24.250
They're pals.

2153
01:48:24.670 --> 01:48:27.370
He reached out to him and he was like, can we use this?

2154
01:48:28.350 --> 01:48:32.230
And at first, John Mayer was like, I don't think so.

2155
01:48:32.410 --> 01:48:32.630
What?

2156
01:48:33.250 --> 01:48:35.710
He told his friend, uh-uh, not happening?

2157
01:48:36.730 --> 01:48:38.270
He was like, I don't think so.

2158
01:48:38.350 --> 01:48:40.750
And he actually wrote about this on his blog.

2159
01:48:41.230 --> 01:48:46.390
He was like, one of my favorite shows on television, The Office, wanted to use my song,

2160
01:48:46.490 --> 01:48:49.490
Your Body is a Wonderland, in a scene for their Christmas episode.

2161
01:48:50.170 --> 01:48:55.150
And he was like, now, I'm not making apologies for my work, but it's safe to say I don't get

2162
01:48:55.150 --> 01:48:59.930
asked to use Wonderland for strongman competitions and documentaries about aircraft carriers.

2163
01:48:59.930 --> 01:49:03.470
I usually get asked so that people can goof on it.

2164
01:49:03.610 --> 01:49:06.310
So I initially turned down the requeSt.

2165
01:49:07.450 --> 01:49:12.990
But after thinking about it, I decided to go for it, but with one stipulation.

2166
01:49:13.250 --> 01:49:14.270
What was it?

2167
01:49:15.190 --> 01:49:17.670
He wrote, I want a Dundee.

2168
01:49:20.200 --> 01:49:25.000
So BJ presented him with a Dundee for tallest music dude.

2169
01:49:25.260 --> 01:49:26.460
He is very tall.

2170
01:49:26.620 --> 01:49:27.440
He's very tall.

2171
01:49:27.440 --> 01:49:30.060
And then he agreed to let us use the song.

2172
01:49:30.060 --> 01:49:31.460
Well, look, I get it.

2173
01:49:31.760 --> 01:49:34.660
Andy and Michael are being total idiots in this episode.

2174
01:49:34.660 --> 01:49:39.720
And so do you want your song to be the song the two idiots picked, right?

2175
01:49:39.960 --> 01:49:40.140
Right.

2176
01:49:40.320 --> 01:49:41.100
But he agreed.

2177
01:49:41.200 --> 01:49:44.520
And Angela, we have a very fun story about John Mayer.

2178
01:49:44.620 --> 01:49:50.020
We danced at the Walk Hard premiere party with John Mayer, and you were very pregnant.

2179
01:49:50.280 --> 01:49:55.780
Look, this is like true BFF friendship, because I did not feel like being in a dress or in any

2180
01:49:55.780 --> 01:49:56.600
kind of fancy shoes.

2181
01:49:56.600 --> 01:49:59.720
But this was a big premiere for you, and I was so excited to celebrate it.

2182
01:50:00.400 --> 01:50:04.060
And then, of course, because you and I have to, we had to dance.

2183
01:50:04.240 --> 01:50:06.700
Listen, I left the after party before 10 p.m.

2184
01:50:06.760 --> 01:50:07.720
I was like, I'm out.

2185
01:50:07.880 --> 01:50:12.000
But I was going to have one dance with my best friend at her big movie premiere.

2186
01:50:12.720 --> 01:50:16.700
And John Mayer was on the dance floor, and he was dancing with someone.

2187
01:50:16.860 --> 01:50:21.700
And I'll never forget, he turned around, and I'm sure he was really surprised to see

2188
01:50:21.700 --> 01:50:25.760
a huge pregnant woman, like directly behind him.

2189
01:50:25.760 --> 01:50:29.120
And he was like, oh my gosh, he goes, you're so beautiful.

2190
01:50:29.640 --> 01:50:34.620
And then he touched my belly, and he said, blessings, blessings.

2191
01:50:36.820 --> 01:50:38.460
I will never forget it.

2192
01:50:38.640 --> 01:50:40.060
My belly was blessed by John Mayer.

2193
01:50:40.440 --> 01:50:44.180
And John, thank you from us for letting us use your song.

2194
01:50:44.400 --> 01:50:44.660
Yeah.

2195
01:50:45.620 --> 01:50:48.060
And he said he still has his dundee, by the way.

2196
01:50:48.200 --> 01:50:49.200
He still has it.

2197
01:50:49.340 --> 01:50:50.880
He better still have his dundee.

2198
01:50:51.540 --> 01:50:52.920
I have both of mine.

2199
01:50:53.680 --> 01:50:54.800
I have both of mine.

2200
01:50:55.420 --> 01:50:59.780
So now we have the scene where Michael is over with Roy and Kevin, and he's kind of

2201
01:50:59.780 --> 01:51:04.980
trying to brag about his new girlfriend, but it's very clear that he doesn't know which

2202
01:51:04.980 --> 01:51:06.140
one is Nikki.

2203
01:51:06.500 --> 01:51:06.640
Right.

2204
01:51:06.820 --> 01:51:08.800
Kevin and Roy are like, you don't know?

2205
01:51:08.980 --> 01:51:09.980
You should know.

2206
01:51:10.360 --> 01:51:12.140
Michael, you should know.

2207
01:51:13.240 --> 01:51:17.020
This leads Michael to really spin out.

2208
01:51:17.260 --> 01:51:20.760
He needs to figure out which woman is his girlfriend.

2209
01:51:20.760 --> 01:51:28.280
So he goes into the kitchen, and he does this whole elaborate bit where he's like, where's

2210
01:51:28.280 --> 01:51:28.980
my girlfriend?

2211
01:51:29.760 --> 01:51:31.240
Where is she?

2212
01:51:31.700 --> 01:51:33.560
Is she in the refrigerator?

2213
01:51:34.520 --> 01:51:42.340
And it's such this awkward moment where finally Nikki says, Michael, you know where I am.

2214
01:51:42.480 --> 01:51:43.780
I'm right here.

2215
01:51:44.380 --> 01:51:51.740
So then when Michael goes in for a hug, he takes out a pen and he marks Nikki's arm because

2216
01:51:51.740 --> 01:51:57.040
this is now how he's going to be able to determine which one of these women is his girlfriend.

2217
01:51:57.040 --> 01:51:59.500
And Angela, this moment really made me cringe.

2218
01:51:59.500 --> 01:52:02.160
Yeah, it made me cringe, too.

2219
01:52:02.560 --> 01:52:06.260
I just don't think the storyline would have been written today.

2220
01:52:07.120 --> 01:52:08.940
Yeah, I don't think so either.

2221
01:52:09.760 --> 01:52:11.700
All right, well, let's get back to the party.

2222
01:52:12.000 --> 01:52:13.380
It's going really well.

2223
01:52:13.660 --> 01:52:15.080
Everyone's having a better time.

2224
01:52:15.700 --> 01:52:21.320
Karen and Jim exchange Bridget Jones' diary, and Jim told us a story about that.

2225
01:52:21.700 --> 01:52:23.700
Yes, and Pam gives Toby a robe.

2226
01:52:24.200 --> 01:52:25.960
Where she got it, I don't know.

2227
01:52:26.200 --> 01:52:27.200
Maybe it's her robe.

2228
01:52:27.880 --> 01:52:29.280
That was a fan theory.

2229
01:52:29.500 --> 01:52:31.140
That Pam gives Toby her robe.

2230
01:52:31.320 --> 01:52:31.980
I like that.

2231
01:52:32.160 --> 01:52:32.320
Yeah.

2232
01:52:32.540 --> 01:52:36.800
And that's when the waitresses decide to leave, though.

2233
01:52:37.100 --> 01:52:37.860
She's like, you know what?

2234
01:52:37.880 --> 01:52:41.000
This party kind of sucks, and we're going to take off.

2235
01:52:41.740 --> 01:52:43.820
And Michael's like, no, don't go.

2236
01:52:44.080 --> 01:52:44.580
Don't go.

2237
01:52:44.820 --> 01:52:46.180
She's like, I'm going to go.

2238
01:52:46.580 --> 01:52:50.740
And that's when he invites her on a trip to Sandals, Jamaica.

2239
01:52:51.000 --> 01:52:51.660
It's all inclusive.

2240
01:52:52.240 --> 01:52:55.000
He is determined to get someone to go on this trip.

2241
01:52:55.000 --> 01:52:58.980
That is the third person in one day he is asked to go.

2242
01:52:59.320 --> 01:53:00.360
He asked Carol.

2243
01:53:00.600 --> 01:53:01.460
He asked Pam.

2244
01:53:01.700 --> 01:53:04.920
And now he's asked Nikki, the waitress.

2245
01:53:06.020 --> 01:53:06.280
Yeah.

2246
01:53:06.460 --> 01:53:10.520
But she's like, no, I think I'm just going to take my bike and get out of here.

2247
01:53:10.720 --> 01:53:11.780
Get out of your lame party.

2248
01:53:12.700 --> 01:53:14.640
I really love that she takes the bike.

2249
01:53:14.640 --> 01:53:15.380
Oh, I do, too.

2250
01:53:17.420 --> 01:53:19.980
She's like, I have this bike, at leaSt.

2251
01:53:20.200 --> 01:53:20.340
Yeah.

2252
01:53:21.140 --> 01:53:24.860
So Michael is devastated, and he's on the couch with Jim.

2253
01:53:25.060 --> 01:53:26.880
And Michael is really mopey.

2254
01:53:27.000 --> 01:53:28.380
He's like, she was the one.

2255
01:53:28.520 --> 01:53:30.580
She was my true love, and she's gone.

2256
01:53:30.640 --> 01:53:33.160
And Jim is like, you barely knew her.

2257
01:53:33.260 --> 01:53:34.340
You knew her for three hours.

2258
01:53:34.500 --> 01:53:35.360
She's not the one.

2259
01:53:35.700 --> 01:53:37.520
She was a rebound.

2260
01:53:37.760 --> 01:53:40.220
And Michael's like, oh, my God, a rebound.

2261
01:53:41.300 --> 01:53:42.580
And Jim's like, yeah.

2262
01:53:42.580 --> 01:53:48.060
And he goes on to say, which, don't get me wrong, can be a great distraction.

2263
01:53:48.380 --> 01:53:54.140
But when it's over, you're left thinking about the girl you really like, the one who broke your heart.

2264
01:53:54.360 --> 01:53:57.340
And Jim is, I mean, we know who Jim's talking about in that moment.

2265
01:53:57.760 --> 01:53:59.940
He's talking about him and Pam.

2266
01:54:00.220 --> 01:54:05.340
And he's basically saying Karen's a rebound, just like Nikki was a rebound.

2267
01:54:06.980 --> 01:54:07.500
Yeah.

2268
01:54:07.860 --> 01:54:12.080
But all Michael hears is that he's had a rebound, and he's super excited.

2269
01:54:12.080 --> 01:54:12.680
Yeah.

2270
01:54:13.640 --> 01:54:14.960
But Jim, we hear you.

2271
01:54:15.240 --> 01:54:15.940
We hear you.

2272
01:54:15.940 --> 01:54:16.680
We hear you, Jim.

2273
01:54:16.880 --> 01:54:17.620
We hear you.

2274
01:54:17.900 --> 01:54:18.900
You love Pam.

2275
01:54:19.080 --> 01:54:19.540
We hear you.

2276
01:54:20.580 --> 01:54:23.940
Now, Angela, we need to discuss Little Drummer Boy.

2277
01:54:24.260 --> 01:54:24.700
Okay.

2278
01:54:26.600 --> 01:54:30.140
We had a fan question from Amanda Gervais.

2279
01:54:30.460 --> 01:54:30.820
Hmm.

2280
01:54:31.160 --> 01:54:31.440
Hey.

2281
01:54:31.580 --> 01:54:31.720
Hey.

2282
01:54:31.980 --> 01:54:40.960
Spelled differently than Ricky Gervais, but she wants to know, how was it decided that Dwight should hold the microphone for Angela?

2283
01:54:41.620 --> 01:54:45.700
I found this choice really interesting because they don't want to look like they're dating,

2284
01:54:46.040 --> 01:54:53.720
but this was kind of the first impression that they gave of interacting in a personal way in front of the entire office.

2285
01:54:54.940 --> 01:54:57.200
Well, here's my story.

2286
01:54:58.000 --> 01:55:01.780
I was terrified to sing this song in front of everyone.

2287
01:55:01.780 --> 01:55:04.960
I do not like singing in front of people.

2288
01:55:05.020 --> 01:55:08.020
I just am not comfortable singing in front of people.

2289
01:55:08.180 --> 01:55:12.440
It's kind of crazy to my whole family because I will do improv.

2290
01:55:12.440 --> 01:55:13.600
I'll do stand-up.

2291
01:55:13.720 --> 01:55:15.020
I'll do crazy sketch comedy.

2292
01:55:15.080 --> 01:55:16.620
I'll be all these weird characters.

2293
01:55:17.060 --> 01:55:20.720
I have no fear ever getting up on stage.

2294
01:55:20.880 --> 01:55:25.660
But if you want me to sing in front of people, it's like I shut down.

2295
01:55:25.840 --> 01:55:28.560
Like my brain computer is like, I can't do it.

2296
01:55:29.400 --> 01:55:36.080
And there's been a few times in my career when I've had to do this, and this was the first time, and I was terrified.

2297
01:55:37.300 --> 01:55:44.060
And I'll never forget, I went up to Harold Ramis, who you guys, you know, we've said he was just a teddy bear.

2298
01:55:44.380 --> 01:55:48.180
And I went up to him, and I was like, here's the thing, Harold.

2299
01:55:48.440 --> 01:55:51.080
I can't do it.

2300
01:55:51.480 --> 01:55:52.440
I can't do it.

2301
01:55:52.520 --> 01:55:57.680
I really just can't sing in front of people, and I can't do it.

2302
01:55:57.680 --> 01:56:05.500
And he really calmly put his hand on my back and looked at me and said, but you will.

2303
01:56:06.680 --> 01:56:12.590
Oh, I'm doing it.

2304
01:56:12.710 --> 01:56:13.710
I am doing it.

2305
01:56:13.850 --> 01:56:19.710
But Angela, I looked in the script, and this bit of Dwight holding the microphone is not in the script.

2306
01:56:19.710 --> 01:56:21.010
So how did that happen?

2307
01:56:21.310 --> 01:56:23.290
I shared with Rain how scared I was.

2308
01:56:23.710 --> 01:56:28.010
You know, we did a take or two where the microphone was on a stand, you know?

2309
01:56:28.510 --> 01:56:34.610
And I'm standing holding my hands, like in this very sort of like, I don't know, I'm clutching my hands.

2310
01:56:34.930 --> 01:56:35.130
Very prim and proper.

2311
01:56:35.270 --> 01:56:38.010
Very prim and proper, clutching my hands in front of my cheSt.

2312
01:56:38.190 --> 01:56:40.730
This was an idea that Jen had, you know?

2313
01:56:40.850 --> 01:56:48.210
And so I'm standing like this because she was saying that she thought I should look like I'm in a very serious church choir stance or something, you know?

2314
01:56:48.830 --> 01:56:49.230
Okay.

2315
01:56:49.230 --> 01:56:52.970
So I'm standing like that, and you guys, I was so nervous.

2316
01:56:52.970 --> 01:56:57.490
I was digging my fingernails into the skin of my other hand.

2317
01:56:57.650 --> 01:57:03.070
I had marks on my hands where I was just like, like death gripping myself.

2318
01:57:03.770 --> 01:57:06.630
And after the first take, I showed Rain my hands.

2319
01:57:06.770 --> 01:57:08.150
I was like, look what I'm doing.

2320
01:57:08.250 --> 01:57:09.030
I'm so nervous.

2321
01:57:09.530 --> 01:57:15.870
And Rain, you know, listen, he just came through for me, you guys.

2322
01:57:16.210 --> 01:57:17.910
Just came through for me.

2323
01:57:17.910 --> 01:57:20.870
I was having a hard time, even though I know the song.

2324
01:57:20.990 --> 01:57:22.870
I was so nervous, and everyone was looking at me.

2325
01:57:22.990 --> 01:57:24.810
I was having a hard time staying on beat.

2326
01:57:25.150 --> 01:57:29.190
And he dropped, he took the microphone, he improvised this.

2327
01:57:29.410 --> 01:57:31.670
He took the microphone, he dropped to his knee.

2328
01:57:31.910 --> 01:57:36.230
And to help me, like, find the song, he's just started going.

2329
01:57:41.190 --> 01:57:43.230
And all of a sudden, I wasn't alone.

2330
01:57:44.050 --> 01:57:45.010
Rain was with me.

2331
01:57:45.310 --> 01:57:46.910
I mean, Rain is six foot three.

2332
01:57:46.910 --> 01:57:49.390
So when he's kneeling down, he's almost my height.

2333
01:57:49.550 --> 01:57:52.110
It was like he was standing side by side with me.

2334
01:57:52.450 --> 01:57:54.050
And then I could do it.

2335
01:57:54.150 --> 01:57:58.290
And you see, if you watch ever so slightly, you see me smile.

2336
01:57:58.510 --> 01:58:03.190
I'm not smiling because Angela loves Dwight, and she's getting to sing a Christmas song.

2337
01:58:03.610 --> 01:58:11.070
I'm smiling because Angela Kinsey sees her friend Rain Wilson come through for her.

2338
01:58:11.070 --> 01:58:15.310
Well, lady, I knew that story, and I was there when it happened.

2339
01:58:15.750 --> 01:58:23.970
And when I watched this scene, I 100% saw that this was a scene between Angela Kinsey and Rain Wilson.

2340
01:58:24.270 --> 01:58:24.410
Yeah.

2341
01:58:24.410 --> 01:58:31.430
The way he's supporting you and the way you're smiling at him, it is so wonderful.

2342
01:58:31.430 --> 01:58:40.650
And then it translates into this moment between Dwight and Angela that just enriches that relationship.

2343
01:58:41.670 --> 01:58:44.230
What a wonderful, wonderful moment.

2344
01:58:44.410 --> 01:58:45.210
It really is.

2345
01:58:45.630 --> 01:58:51.450
Anyway, so Rain, thank you so much for coming through for me with your bums and getting me through that scene.

2346
01:58:51.450 --> 01:59:00.410
Now, during all of this, Angela, Oscar and Gil walk into the party, and he's like, too soon.

2347
01:59:00.610 --> 01:59:02.410
What brilliant timing, though.

2348
01:59:02.610 --> 01:59:04.810
I mean, that was such a well-written moment.

2349
01:59:05.090 --> 01:59:08.790
Here he is making his return to work.

2350
01:59:08.930 --> 01:59:10.870
You know, he's bringing his boyfriend.

2351
01:59:11.610 --> 01:59:12.390
That's it.

2352
01:59:12.650 --> 01:59:14.330
Oscar is back, right?

2353
01:59:14.330 --> 01:59:21.650
And then he sees Angela, of all people, singing Little Drummer Boy, and he just does a pivot.

2354
01:59:21.830 --> 01:59:23.230
He's like, nope, not happening.

2355
01:59:23.910 --> 01:59:29.790
Also during this, in the background, we see Roy give Pam a Christmas gift.

2356
01:59:29.830 --> 01:59:35.450
And we had some people write in to ask, what book did Roy get Pam for Christmas?

2357
01:59:35.850 --> 01:59:37.830
Was it a really thoughtful gift?

2358
01:59:37.830 --> 01:59:45.830
This was asked by Juliette Wilson, Donna Miller, Celia Quiggle, Demetra Lizu, Sarah Thorpe, Sarah Fletcher, and Brooke Beagle.

2359
01:59:46.410 --> 01:59:48.310
A lot of people want to know what the present was.

2360
01:59:48.610 --> 01:59:50.650
You guys, it was an art book.

2361
01:59:50.810 --> 01:59:53.110
It was a very thoughtful present.

2362
01:59:53.470 --> 01:59:54.670
Roy is winning me over.

2363
01:59:55.090 --> 01:59:58.890
He wasn't the best boyfriend and fiance, but he's really trying.

2364
01:59:59.090 --> 02:00:02.650
He's, you know, invested in how to learn how to gift wrap.

2365
02:00:02.650 --> 02:00:10.410
And he's dressing nicer, and he's getting in shape, and he is like, I'm going to buy you a thoughtful gift.

2366
02:00:10.570 --> 02:00:11.130
And, ugh.

2367
02:00:13.660 --> 02:00:14.140
I know.

2368
02:00:15.080 --> 02:00:16.300
This was intentional.

2369
02:00:16.680 --> 02:00:21.540
There was a part of the season where I thought Pam might be won over by Roy.

2370
02:00:21.760 --> 02:00:24.080
And they weren't even sure in the writer's room, right?

2371
02:00:24.080 --> 02:00:25.120
They hadn't decided.

2372
02:00:25.180 --> 02:00:25.400
No.

2373
02:00:26.300 --> 02:00:40.340
No, I had this whole conversation with Greg where I was like, Greg, wouldn't it be, like, a crazy, crazy thing if the real true love story is Pam and Roy?

2374
02:00:40.780 --> 02:00:55.060
Like, what if all this time Jim is just a device that leads Pam to her real true love of Roy, and Roy completely rehabilitates himself, and that's the love story of The Office.

2375
02:00:55.060 --> 02:00:56.660
It would blow people's minds.

2376
02:00:57.020 --> 02:01:00.420
And Greg was kind of like, yeah, I hear what you're saying.

2377
02:01:00.460 --> 02:01:02.940
I also think it's going to be Jim and Pam.

2378
02:01:03.680 --> 02:01:09.360
But I was like, I'm just saying, if we really want to shock people, maybe it's Pam and Roy.

2379
02:01:09.840 --> 02:01:11.600
And he was like, yeah, I don't know.

2380
02:01:11.760 --> 02:01:13.920
There are people listening right now and are like, no!

2381
02:01:15.340 --> 02:01:16.020
I know.

2382
02:01:16.280 --> 02:01:19.320
So instead of jam fans, there would have been poi fans?

2383
02:01:19.480 --> 02:01:20.380
Poi fans?

2384
02:01:23.890 --> 02:01:24.750
Ram fans.

2385
02:01:24.870 --> 02:01:25.470
Ram fans.

2386
02:01:25.470 --> 02:01:30.450
Well, ultimately, I do believe that it was always going to be Jim and Pam.

2387
02:01:30.930 --> 02:01:33.130
But we had to, Blake, pause.

2388
02:01:33.390 --> 02:01:34.070
We had a moment.

2389
02:01:34.090 --> 02:01:36.970
I think partially because David Denman's performance.

2390
02:01:36.970 --> 02:01:40.350
We were all a little bit falling in love with Roy right now.

2391
02:01:40.530 --> 02:01:40.790
Yeah.

2392
02:01:40.970 --> 02:01:42.450
Yeah, he did a great job.

2393
02:01:42.650 --> 02:01:46.990
I think it was such an excellent foil to see Roy step it up, you know?

2394
02:01:47.410 --> 02:01:50.050
And I think that needed to happen.

2395
02:01:50.050 --> 02:01:56.450
I think Mindy sort of touched on that when she was a guest that, like, we needed to see Roy, like, really make a go of it.

2396
02:01:56.450 --> 02:01:57.590
Yeah.

2397
02:01:58.010 --> 02:01:59.550
Well, I want to say something.

2398
02:02:00.370 --> 02:02:01.590
What's up with Jim?

2399
02:02:02.270 --> 02:02:04.630
Jim clocks this through the window.

2400
02:02:05.530 --> 02:02:10.310
And then all of a sudden, he's like, hey, Pam, I want to do your CIA joke.

2401
02:02:10.310 --> 02:02:11.730
Oh, do you, Jim?

2402
02:02:12.210 --> 02:02:12.990
You do.

2403
02:02:13.750 --> 02:02:15.050
Interesting timing.

2404
02:02:15.510 --> 02:02:16.110
Well.

2405
02:02:16.110 --> 02:02:18.570
That you're suddenly invested in the CIA joke.

2406
02:02:18.770 --> 02:02:20.730
Why couldn't he have just left well enough alone?

2407
02:02:21.950 --> 02:02:23.590
Well, Pam was delighted.

2408
02:02:23.910 --> 02:02:25.990
It literally saved the day for her.

2409
02:02:26.950 --> 02:02:28.390
Yeah, she was thrilled.

2410
02:02:28.870 --> 02:02:30.270
And it's very fun.

2411
02:02:30.470 --> 02:02:36.090
They decide that they're going to tell Dwight that a helicopter will be picking him up.

2412
02:02:37.740 --> 02:02:39.560
And he goes up to the roof.

2413
02:02:40.320 --> 02:02:42.780
And then they play that final prank on him.

2414
02:02:43.100 --> 02:02:43.740
I know.

2415
02:02:43.860 --> 02:02:46.600
And then he throws his phone off the roof.

2416
02:02:47.420 --> 02:02:47.960
Dwight.

2417
02:02:48.140 --> 02:02:48.440
Amazing.

2418
02:02:48.740 --> 02:02:49.160
Dwight.

2419
02:02:49.500 --> 02:02:50.380
Come on, buddy.

2420
02:02:50.680 --> 02:03:00.560
Well, we can't end this episode without the major cliffhanger, which is that we spot Michael on the phone in his office inviting someone, a fourth person to Jamaica.

2421
02:03:01.500 --> 02:03:02.840
And they say yes.

2422
02:03:02.860 --> 02:03:04.380
And the look on his face.

2423
02:03:04.380 --> 02:03:05.960
He's like, oh, OK.

2424
02:03:06.340 --> 02:03:07.880
Like, oh, my God.

2425
02:03:08.060 --> 02:03:10.660
But who he has called, we don't know.

2426
02:03:10.880 --> 02:03:14.240
It will be revealed next week in Back From Vacation.

2427
02:03:14.240 --> 02:03:20.000
I remember at the table read for this, when he read that last line, there was such a buzz in the room.

2428
02:03:20.120 --> 02:03:20.740
They're like, whoa.

2429
02:03:21.620 --> 02:03:22.640
We know who it is.

2430
02:03:22.640 --> 02:03:23.220
We know.

2431
02:03:23.400 --> 02:03:24.700
But you guys know.

2432
02:03:24.940 --> 02:03:27.020
And next week, we'll talk all about it.

2433
02:03:27.020 --> 02:03:28.180
Well, that's it.

2434
02:03:28.620 --> 02:03:30.140
We had a Benihana Christmas.

2435
02:03:30.420 --> 02:03:31.420
We had awesome guests.

2436
02:03:31.560 --> 02:03:32.360
Thank you, Rashida.

2437
02:03:32.520 --> 02:03:33.120
Thank you, Jen.

2438
02:03:33.320 --> 02:03:34.760
And thanks, you guys, for listening.

2439
02:03:35.100 --> 02:03:36.200
Yeah, we'll see you next week.

2440
